{
  "requirement": "For a requirements input, `requirements` MUST be a {term}`requirements.references.definition_selection`, and Habeas MUST match it against all defined requirements and named examples. It MUST recompute the matches during validation, sort their full names, and compare them with `matches`. It MUST take each match's complete raw fenced declaration, including its opening and closing lines, concatenate those declarations in full-name order with one blank line between them, and compare the resulting raw lines with `text`. It MUST retain every match's current source file and inclusive line range for display and reference coverage. A selection matching no definitions MUST be invalid. Adding, removing, renaming, or changing a matched definition MUST invalidate the stored input; moving an unchanged declaration within the book MUST NOT. Errors MUST identify the selection and affected definitions when available.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "Nearly every obligation is implemented and tested. One obligation is verified only by a test that carries no `{test}` reference to the subject, so I judge that a marking gap.\n\n**Obligations, code and tests**\n- **`requirements` MUST be a definition selection.**\n  - Code: `InputSelector::resolve`, `Requirements` arm (src/inputs.rs:244), calls `definition_glob::validate`.\n  - Test: `requirements_inputs_track_matched_declarations_in_full_name_order` (src/evidence.rs:2510) rejects `foo.[a].bar` and the empty selection.\n- **Match against all requirements and named examples.**\n  - Code: `resolve` skips `DefinitionKind::Term` and uses `definition_glob::matches`.\n  - Tests: the same test, plus tests/definitions.rs `selections_match_requirements_and_examples_but_never_named_definitions`.\n- **Recompute matches, sort by full name, compare with `matches`.**\n  - Code: `resolve` iterates the `BTreeMap`, which is sorted. `validate_resolved_input` (src/evidence.rs:947) compares and reports \"matches changed; added …, removed …\".\n  - Test: the full-name-order test, where `foo.a.b.bar` sorts before `foo.a.bar`.\n- **Take each complete raw fenced declaration, concatenate in full-name order with one blank line, compare with `text`.**\n  - Code: `collect_definitions` stores `raw_lines` (src/evidence.rs:413). `resolve` joins them with an empty line, and `validate_resolved_input` compares `text != resolved.text`.\n  - Tests: the full-name-order test, `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates`, and `requirements_inputs_omit_option_lines`.\n- **A selection matching nothing MUST be invalid.**\n  - Code: the `matches.is_empty()` error in `resolve`.\n  - Test: the `foo.*.none` case, and tests/definitions.rs for an exact name selecting a named definition.\n- **Adding, removing, renaming or changing a matched definition invalidates the input; moving an unchanged declaration does not.**\n  - Test: the full-name-order test covers all five cases. It adds `foo.z.bar`, removes the nested example, renames `a.bar` to `c.bar`, changes `Bar.` to `Changed.`, and reorders the declarations with prose between them. The cited-example test also covers adding.\n- **Errors MUST identify the selection and affected definitions.**\n  - Code: the messages name the glob, the added and removed names, and `changed definitions […]` plus a diff.\n  - Test: asserted in the full-name-order test.\n\n**Gap: retaining each match's source file and inclusive line range**\n- Code: `resolve` builds `ranges` as `SourceRange` values with file and line start/end. `render_input` displays them and `evidence_input_ranges` uses them for reference coverage.\n- No test marked `{test}``requirements.ci.requirements_inputs`` asserts the retained ranges.\n  - `requirements_inputs_omit_option_lines` asserts `Declaration` line numbers and the resolved text, not `resolved.ranges`.\n  - The full-name-order test and the cited-example test do not assert ranges either.\n- Two unmarked tests do verify this obligation:\n  - src/index.rs `detail_page_shows_recorded_text_locations_and_first_matching_group` asserts that a requirements input lists \"each match's name, file, and inclusive range\" (`md/rules.md:5–7`, `md/rules.md:1–3`). It is marked only `requirements.index.detail_format` and `requirements.definitions.inputs`.\n  - src/evidence.rs `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` covers coverage only for an outline input on `src/main.rs`. No test shows a requirements input's range covering a reference in the book.\n- A test that verifies the subject without a `{test}` reference to it is a marking gap.\n- No `{fixme}` acknowledges this gap.",
  "references": "e36826c65524e8bed9847487c2e4439ebfb2400ca4e19fe2a2c974379843c895",
